
/*
QUERY NAME: EMS 5681–5684 Gradebook Items and Final Grades
            for 2023 and 2024 Courses

PURPOSE:
Retrieves Blackboard Learn gradebook information for
EMS 5681, EMS 5682, EMS 5683, and EMS 5684 courses
whose course identifiers contain 2023 or 2024.

The query identifies all qualifying gradebook items,
including those designated as External/Final Grades.

It provides information about gradebook item names,
descriptions, possible points, due dates, visibility,
grade calculation settings, grade release status,
and creation/modification dates.

This report can be used to review and compare gradebook
configurations across the selected EMS courses.

DATA SOURCES:

1. CDM_LMS.COURSE (c)
   Contains Blackboard course information, including
   course identifiers, course names, course numbers,
   and STAGE JSON data.

2. CDM_LMS.GRADEBOOK (gb)
   Contains course gradebook items, assessment settings,
   possible scores, due dates, visibility indicators,
   and final grade identification.

TABLE RELATIONSHIP:

GRADEBOOK.COURSE_ID = COURSE.ID

An INNER JOIN connects each gradebook item to its
corresponding Blackboard course.

IMPORTANT:
- Only courses with matching gradebook records
  are included.
- A course can have multiple gradebook items.
- Each qualifying gradebook item produces a
  separate result row.
- Courses with no qualifying gradebook items
  do not appear in the results.

------------------------------------------------------------
FIELDS RETURNED
------------------------------------------------------------

COURSE INFORMATION:

1. course_surrogate_id
   Internal unique course identifier from COURSE.ID.

2. course_number
   Course number stored in CDM_LMS.COURSE.

3. blackboard_course_id
   Extracts batch_uid from the COURSE.STAGE JSON field.

   c.stage:batch_uid::string

   The ::string conversion returns the JSON value
   as a text string.

   This field may contain NULL when batch_uid
   is not present in the STAGE data.

4. course_name
   Blackboard course name.

GRADEBOOK INFORMATION:

5. gradebook_id
   Internal unique identifier for the gradebook item.

6. gradebook_source_id
   Source system identifier for the gradebook item.

7. gradebook_item_name
   Name of the gradebook column or item.

8. gradebook_item_description
   Description associated with the gradebook item.

9. gradebook_type
   Gradebook item type stored in Blackboard Data.

10. possible_score
    Maximum possible points associated with the
    gradebook item.

11. due_time
    Scheduled due date/time for the gradebook item,
    when defined.

12. visible_ind
    Indicates the gradebook item's visibility
    according to the stored indicator.

13. used_in_calculations_ind
    Indicates whether the gradebook item is marked
    for use in grade calculations.

14. grades_released_ind
    Indicates whether grades are marked as released.

15. final_grade_ind
    Identifies gradebook columns designated as
    final grade columns.

    A value of 1 indicates a final grade designation.

GRADEBOOK ITEM CLASSIFICATION:

16. gradebook_item_type

    Uses a CASE statement to identify whether
    each gradebook item is designated as a final
    grade column.

    CASE
        WHEN gb.final_grade_ind = 1
            THEN 'EXTERNAL / FINAL GRADE'
        ELSE 'GRADEBOOK ITEM'
    END

    Classification:

    final_grade_ind = 1:
        EXTERNAL / FINAL GRADE

    All other values:
        GRADEBOOK ITEM

    IMPORTANT:
    This classification is based entirely on
    GRADEBOOK.FINAL_GRADE_IND.

    It does not independently verify Blackboard's
    External Grade designation or grading policy.

GRADEBOOK TIMESTAMPS:

17. created_time
    Date/time when the gradebook item was created.

18. modified_time
    Date/time when the gradebook item was last modified,
    as recorded in Blackboard Data.

------------------------------------------------------------
FILTERING CONDITIONS
------------------------------------------------------------

1. gb.deleted_ind = 0

   Excludes gradebook items marked as deleted
   using the DELETED_IND indicator.

2. gb.row_deleted_time IS NULL

   Excludes gradebook records with a populated
   deletion timestamp.

3. c.row_deleted_time IS NULL

   Excludes courses marked as deleted.

IMPORTANT:
The query applies deletion filtering to both
the course and gradebook records.

However, it does not check whether the courses
are currently available or enabled.

------------------------------------------------------------
EMS COURSE FILTER
------------------------------------------------------------

The query searches for course identifiers containing:

- EMS_5681
- EMS_5682
- EMS_5683
- EMS_5684

It uses:

COALESCE(c.stage:batch_uid::string, c.course_number)

This expression selects:

1. The COURSE.STAGE batch_uid when it is not NULL.
2. The COURSE.COURSE_NUMBER when batch_uid is NULL.

IMPORTANT:
COALESCE does not search both fields independently.

If batch_uid contains a non-NULL value, course_number
is not evaluated as an alternative for matching.

UPPER():
Converts the selected identifier to uppercase.

LIKE:
Searches the uppercase identifier for the
specified EMS course patterns.

The percent signs (%) allow additional characters
before and after the matching pattern.

IMPORTANT:
In SQL LIKE patterns, underscores (_) are
single-character wildcards.

For example, EMS_5681 can match EMS_5681,
but it can also match EMS-5681.

The current query does not require literal
underscore characters.

------------------------------------------------------------
ACADEMIC YEAR FILTER
------------------------------------------------------------

The query restricts results to course identifiers
containing either:

- 2023
- 2024

It uses:

COALESCE(c.stage:batch_uid::string, c.course_number)

The same identifier selection rules apply:

- Use batch_uid if available.
- Otherwise use course_number.

LIKE '%2023%':
Matches identifiers containing 2023 anywhere.

LIKE '%2024%':
Matches identifiers containing 2024 anywhere.

IMPORTANT:
The filter searches identifier text.

It does not use:
- COURSE.START_DATE
- COURSE.END_DATE
- COURSE.TERM_ID
- CDM_LMS.TERM

Therefore, 2023 and 2024 refer to text found
in the selected course identifier rather than
verified academic years.

------------------------------------------------------------
COMBINED FILTERING LOGIC
------------------------------------------------------------

To appear in the results, a record must meet
all of the following conditions:

1. The course is not marked as deleted.

2. The gradebook item is not marked as deleted.

3. The selected course identifier contains
   one of the four EMS course patterns.

4. The selected course identifier contains
   either 2023 or 2024.

5. The course has at least one matching
   gradebook item.

The EMS filters are combined using OR.

The year filters are also combined using OR.

The two groups are connected using AND.

Therefore, a course must match both:
- One requested EMS course pattern.
- One requested year pattern.

------------------------------------------------------------
GRADEBOOK ITEMS INCLUDED
------------------------------------------------------------

The query does not restrict results exclusively
to final grade columns.

It includes all qualifying gradebook items where
the deletion filters are satisfied.

These may include:
- Assignment gradebook columns.
- Test or quiz gradebook columns.
- Manually created gradebook columns.
- Calculated gradebook columns.
- Columns designated as final grades.

The specific records returned depend on the
gradebook configuration of each course.

The GRADEBOOK_ITEM_TYPE output makes it easier
to distinguish designated final grade columns
from other gradebook items.

------------------------------------------------------------
SORTING
------------------------------------------------------------

Results are ordered by:

1. c.course_number
   Groups records by Blackboard course number
   in ascending order.

2. gb.final_grade_ind DESC
   Displays rows with higher FINAL_GRADE_IND values
   first within each course.

   Normally, items designated as final grades
   will appear before standard gradebook items.

3. gb.name
   Sorts gradebook item names alphabetically
   within the preceding groups.

------------------------------------------------------------
IMPORTANT NOTES
------------------------------------------------------------

- The query searches four EMS course patterns
  across identifiers containing 2023 or 2024.

- The report returns gradebook configuration
  information rather than individual student grades.

- No CDM_LMS.GRADE records are retrieved.

- No student names, student IDs, or earned student
  scores are included.

- A course may appear multiple times because
  each gradebook item produces a separate row.

- Final grade columns are identified using
  GRADEBOOK.FINAL_GRADE_IND = 1.

- The query includes regular gradebook columns
  as well as designated final grade columns.

- Course availability and enabled status
  are not evaluated.

- Gradebook visibility and release indicators
  are returned but are not used as filters.

- No date restrictions are applied to gradebook
  creation, modification, or due dates.

- The year filter searches course identifiers
  rather than official academic term dates.

- The query does not use CURRENT_DATE().

- Results reflect gradebook records available
  in Blackboard Data - Illuminate at query time.

*/

SELECT
    c.id AS course_surrogate_id,
    c.course_number,
    c.stage:batch_uid::string AS blackboard_course_id,
    c.name AS course_name,

    gb.id AS gradebook_id,
    gb.source_id AS gradebook_source_id,
    gb.name AS gradebook_item_name,
    gb.description AS gradebook_item_description,
    gb.gradebook_type,
    gb.possible_score,
    gb.due_time,
    gb.visible_ind,
    gb.used_in_calculations_ind,
    gb.grades_released_ind,
    gb.final_grade_ind,

    CASE
        WHEN gb.final_grade_ind = 1 THEN 'EXTERNAL / FINAL GRADE'
        ELSE 'GRADEBOOK ITEM'
    END AS gradebook_item_type,

    gb.created_time,
    gb.modified_time

FROM CDM_LMS.COURSE c

INNER JOIN CDM_LMS.GRADEBOOK gb
    ON gb.course_id = c.id

WHERE
    gb.deleted_ind = 0
    AND gb.row_deleted_time IS NULL
    AND c.row_deleted_time IS NULL

    -- EMS courses requested
    AND (
        UPPER(COALESCE(c.stage:batch_uid::string, c.course_number)) LIKE '%EMS_5681%'
        OR UPPER(COALESCE(c.stage:batch_uid::string, c.course_number)) LIKE '%EMS_5682%'
        OR UPPER(COALESCE(c.stage:batch_uid::string, c.course_number)) LIKE '%EMS_5683%'
        OR UPPER(COALESCE(c.stage:batch_uid::string, c.course_number)) LIKE '%EMS_5684%'
    )

    -- Only course IDs containing 2023 or 2024
    AND (
        COALESCE(c.stage:batch_uid::string, c.course_number) LIKE '%2023%'
        OR COALESCE(c.stage:batch_uid::string, c.course_number) LIKE '%2024%'
    )

ORDER BY
    c.course_number,
    gb.final_grade_ind DESC,
    gb.name;
